  "question": {
    "text": "Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> are three distinct numbers in arithmetic progression. Also <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> are in geometric progression and <math><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. If <math><mi>l</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo></math> then <math><mi>n</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;are in A.P.&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></math></p><p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Let,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Now,&nbsp;<math><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></math> or <math><mi>l</mi><mi>n</mi></math><br />So <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> or <math><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math> (<math><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is rejected)<br />Hence,&nbsp;<math><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p>"
  }
}